    "closure": "every fiber degree drop is an exact residual parity run on the unique projective scalar-weld vector",
    "statement": "In collision shape A, write the classified split rows as G(t,x)=lambda_x P_x(t), where lambda is the unique projective row-scalar vector from the coefficient-MDS and connected scalar-weld gates. For each off-line slope delta, divide the row values at X_delta=U_0 minus I_delta by the known actual-support and padded factors. The resulting values are zeta_delta H_delta(x). Their exact Reed-Solomon parity run starts at exponent 3e+r_delta-1 and has length q_delta=n-deg_X G(delta,X), followed by the nonzero value zeta_delta lc(H_delta). Hence every degree drop, and therefore deg T=e-sum q_delta, is determined by one explicit stacked linear flag applied to the same lambda; there are no independent fiber residual choices.",
